    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "Add or subtract the fractions and simplify. $\\frac2{x+2}+\\frac3{x-1}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{5x+4}{(x+2)(x-1)}$, $x\\ne-2,1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac2{x+2}+\\frac3{x-1}&=\\frac{2(x-1)+3(x+2)}{(x+2)(x-1)}\\\\\\frac2{x+2}+\\frac3{x-1}&=\\frac{2x-2+3x+6}{(x+2)(x-1)}\\\\\\frac2{x+2}+\\frac3{x-1}&=\\frac{5x+4}{(x+2)(x-1)}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: $x\\ne-2,1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
